      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stafford Springs’ former railroad station sits just 100 feet from the Holt Memorial Fountain, one of the village’s few surviving historic structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stafford_Springs%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Civil War, factories in Stafford Springs churned out cannonballs to support the Union war effort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stafford_Springs%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Founded in 1853, Warren Mills became one of the village’s most prominent operations and is among the oldest continuously running textile mills in the U.S.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stafford_Springs%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village lies near the source of the Willimantic River, whose flow historically powered the mills that shaped Stafford Springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stafford_Springs%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Holt Memorial Fountain sits at the junction of Routes 32, 190 and Furnace Avenue, forming a traffic roundabout described as one of New England’s oldest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stafford_Springs%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Before becoming a town, the land that is now Stafford Springs was originally Mohegan territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
